{
  "schema": "ssam-client-content/1",
  "_doc": [
    "Client content kept out of the release (plan section 7.2 V, decision D7, CRITICA-ADENDO AM6). Only lane V edits this file. It lives only in the publisher repository and is never copied into a release (the scan would flag it).",
    "Paths are relative to the repository root with '/'. builderFeatures, jobs and fixtures are allow-lists: a builder feature, suite job or job base that is not listed never goes into a release.",
    "builderFeatures: the ODC builder features compiled in release. parts/BuilderFeatures.targets removes <folder>/*.cs and includes <folder>/<include> (MSBuild wildcard), only in a release build; files is that wildcard resolved at freeze time (client-content.test.mjs checks both agree).",
    "jobs.neutral: the suite jobs that compile-runtime-data.mjs (lane U) may turn into release data (recipes, discovery, job:<name>, proofs). fixtures.neutral: the only job bases (.oml) that may ship. A file outside fixtures.neutral never ships, nor any field of its sidecar (module, host, developerId, path); its sha256 alone is not a name.",
    "forbidden: what scan-client-content.mjs looks for in every file of a release (DLL, EXE, JSON, JSC, JWS, notices). pattern is a JavaScript regular expression source, matched case-insensitively over each file decoded as Latin-1 and as UTF-16LE at both byte alignments, so it also finds .NET metadata names (UTF-8), .NET string literals (UTF-16) and V8 bytecode strings (one-byte and two-byte). Any match fails the release unless allow covers it.",
    "forbidden[].kind: client | tenant | email | domain | identifier. forbidden[].label: what the term stands for. forbidden[].seen: where the term was found at freeze time (evidence, not the scan scope).",
    "allow: exceptions {path, pattern, why}; path is a glob with '/' relative to the release root, pattern repeats one forbidden pattern exactly. Empty at freeze time.",
    "Names too generic to scan (the client module 'Quotes', business terms such as FEMA or NFIP) stay out only through the allow-lists."
  ],
  "frozenAt": {
    "commit": "4c05f9f4",
    "date": "2026-10-03"
